1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:07,970
DIMNA: Kalila, what if you and five friends were stuck in a hunter's net, and you could never fly home again? What would you do?

2
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:11,480
KALILA: Hmm. I would pull and pull, as hard as I can!

3
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:16,540
DIMNA: All by yourself? Ha! Sit down, brother. Today's story will show you a better way.

4
00:00:21,490 --> 00:00:28,240
Once upon a time, in a green meadow, there stood a tall tree. A crow lived at the top, and he saw everything.

5
00:00:28,690 --> 00:00:35,420
One morning, the crow saw a hunter. The hunter spread a big net on the grass, and he threw grain all over it.

6
00:00:35,970 --> 00:00:40,510
HUNTER: Hee hee. Now I will hide, and wait for some hungry birds.

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:44,140
CROW: Oh no. That is a trap! I must watch and see what happens.

8
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:54,460
Soon, a flock of doves came flying by. Their leader was the Ring-Dove. She had a beautiful golden ring around her neck, and she was very wise.

9
00:00:54,810 --> 00:00:57,050
YOUNG DOVE: Look, everyone! Yummy grain! Let's eat!

10
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:01,480
RING-DOVE: Wait, little ones! Grain in the middle of a meadow? Something is not right...

11
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:08,500
But the young doves were too hungry. Down they flew. And snap! The net closed tight around them all.

12
00:01:08,850 --> 00:01:10,770
YOUNG DOVE: Help! I'm stuck! I can't get out!

13
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:15,590
HUNTER: Ha ha! Look at all those doves! What a lucky day for me!

14
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:22,340
The doves flapped and pulled, each one on its own. But the more they pulled, the tighter the net became.

15
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:32,390
RING-DOVE: Stop! Listen to me, friends! If each of us pulls alone, we will never get free. But if we all fly up together, at the very same time, we can lift this net into the sky!

16
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:35,410
RING-DOVE: Ready? One... two... three... FLY!

17
00:01:35,810 --> 00:01:40,150
And up they went! All together, with the whole net, high into the sky!

18
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,860
HUNTER: Hey! Come back with my net!

19
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:50,680
The hunter ran after them, over the hills and through the fields. And the curious crow followed too.

20
00:01:51,130 --> 00:01:56,960
HUNTER: Huff, puff... They are too fast for me. Oh well. I will go home and have some soup.

21
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:03,390
RING-DOVE: Now, friends, let's fly to my old friend Zirak, the mouse. He will help us.

22
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:06,960
They landed beside a big rock with a little hole in it.

23
00:02:07,410 --> 00:02:10,010
RING-DOVE: Zirak! Zirak, my friend! Are you home?

24
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:14,520
ZIRAK: Who's there? Oh, it's you, my dear Ring-Dove! What happened? Don't worry, I will chew this net for you!

25
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:19,300
RING-DOVE: Thank you, Zirak. But please, free my friends first. Free me last.

26
00:02:19,650 --> 00:02:20,900
ZIRAK: Last? But why?

27
00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:25,840
RING-DOVE: Because I am their leader. If you get tired, I don't want any of them left behind.

28
00:02:26,290 --> 00:02:28,500
ZIRAK: Now I see why your friends love you so much!

29
00:02:28,950 --> 00:02:35,210
Nibble, nibble, nibble! One by one, Zirak set every dove free. And last of all, the Ring-Dove.

30
00:02:37,410 --> 00:02:41,050
CROW: Wow, I saw everything! You help each other! Can I be your friend too?

31
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:44,120
ZIRAK: Hmm... A crow? Well, all right! Friends help friends. Welcome!

32
00:02:44,670 --> 00:02:49,350
And from that day on, the doves, the mouse and the crow were the best of friends.

33
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:56,960
KALILA: So no dove could lift the net alone. But all together, they flew away free!

34
00:02:57,110 --> 00:03:00,790
DIMNA: And the Ring-Dove thought of her friends first. Together, we are strong!

35
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:05,270
DIMNA: Persian word of the day! In Persian, a dove is kabootar. Kabootar!

36
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:09,290
KALILA: Kabootar. A dove. Let's fly together, like the kabootar.

37
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:15,610
KALILA: And next time: a clever crow, a mean snake, and a shiny necklace.

